      "text": "{\"body\":\"## Parent\\n\\n#242 ([PRD] Cross-Module Generalization: Customer Component + Full POS Line Items)\\n\\n## What to build\\n\\nCreate `shared/validations/line-item-variants.ts` containing three reusable variant definition objects (part, labor, bicycle) that each module imports and composes into its own discriminated union schema. Refactor existing schemas (repair, quote, customer-order) to import from the shared variants file instead of duplicating base fields.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `shared/validations/line-item-variants.ts` created with three variant objects:\\n  - Part variant: `{ lineType: 'part', partId (required), description, quantity, unitPriceNet, vatRateId, discountPercent }`\\n  - Labor variant: `{ lineType: 'labor', laborServiceId (nullable), minutesWorked (nullable), hourlyRateSnapshot (nullable), description, quantity, unitPriceNet, vatRateId, discountPercent }`\\n  - Bicycle variant: `{ lineType: 'bicycle', bicycleId (nullable), bicycleBrand/Model/Year/Color/FrameSize (all nullable), description, quantity, unitPriceNet, vatRateId, discountPercent }`\\n- [ ] Existing schemas refactored to import from shared variants: `repair.ts`, `quote.ts`, `customer-order.ts`\\n- [ ] Unit tests for each variant: valid inputs pass, missing required fields fail with correct error messages, nullable fields accept null\\n- [ ] No behavior change \u2014 all existing validation tests still pass\\n\\n## Blocked by\\n\\nNone - can start immediately\\n\\n<!-- AGENT-FINDINGS-START -->\\n## Agent Findings\\n\\n### Archivist \u2014 2026-06-01 (Round 1)\\n\\n#### Semantic Conflict: Required vs Optional/Nullable Across Modules\\n\\nThe issue states `partId (required)` and `laborServiceId (nullable)` for the shared variants, but **existing module semantics differ**:\\n\\n| Field | repair.ts | quote.ts | customer-order.ts |\\n|-------|-----------|----------|-------------------|\\n| `partId` | **required** (`z.string().min(1)`) | optional/nullable UUID | nullable/optional string |\\n| `laborServiceId` | **required** (`z.string().min(1)`) | optional/nullable UUID | nullable/optional string |\\n\\n- **repair.ts** (line 200): `partId: z.string().min(1, 'partId is required')` \u2014 always required for parts\\n- **repair.ts** (line 207): `laborServiceId: z.string().min(1, 'laborServiceId is required')` \u2014 always required for labor\\n- **quote.ts** (line 63): `partId: z.string().uuid('...').optional().nullable()` \u2014 optional/nullable\\n- **quote.ts** (line 69): `laborServiceId: z.string().uuid('...').optional().nullable()` \u2014 optional/nullable\\n\\nThis means a single shared variant definition cannot enforce both semantics simultaneously. The builder needs to decide on one of these approaches:\\n\\n1. **\\\"Loose base\\\" pattern**: Shared variants define all fields as optional/nullable, and each module tightens constraints via `.refine()` or schema composition (e.g., `sharedVariantSchema.extend({ partId: z.string().min(1) })`)\\n2. **Module-specific variant factories**: The shared file exports factory functions that accept a config object specifying requiredness per field\\n3. **Two tiers of variants**: A \\\"strict\\\" tier (repair semantics) and a \\\"loose\\\" tier (quote/order semantics), each composed from the same base\\n\\n#### Existing Code Patterns \u2014 Both Files Already Use `baseLineItemFields` Spread\\n\\nBoth files already have near-identical `baseLineItemFields` objects using object spread into `z.object()`:\\n\\n- **repair.ts** (line 189): `const baseLineItemFields = { description, quantity, unitPriceNet, vatRateId, discountPercent }`\\n- **quote.ts** (line 51): `const baseLineItemFields = { lineType, description, quantity, unitPriceNet, vatRateId, discountPercent }`\\n\\nThese are the natural extraction targets. Note that quote.ts includes `lineType` in the base while repair.ts puts it per-variant.\\n\\n#### customer-order.ts Uses Flat Object (Not Discriminated Union)\\n\\n**customer-order.ts** does NOT use a discriminated union \u2014 it uses a flat `z.object()` with all fields nullable/optional regardless of `lineType`. This is structurally different from repair.ts and quote.ts, meaning the shared variants file would need to support both composition patterns.\\n\\n#### Test Coverage \u2014 Existing Tests Per Module\\n\\n- **`shared/validations/__tests__/quote.test.ts`**: Comprehensive tests for create/update line items across all 3 types (part, labor, bicycle). ~250 lines covering valid inputs, missing required fields, boundary values.\\n- **`shared/validations/repair.test.ts`**: Tests intake schema extensively but does NOT test `createPartLineItemSchema` or `createLaborLineItemSchema`. Line item creation tests are absent.\\n\\n#### Relevant Files Summary\\n\\n| File | Purpose | Key Lines |\\n|------|---------|-----------|\\n| `shared/validations/repair.ts:189-215` | repair line item schemas (part + labor, discriminated union) | baseLineItemFields, createPartLineItemSchema, createLaborLineItemSchema |\\n| `shared/validations/quote.ts:51-83` | quote line item schemas (part + labor + bicycle, discriminated union) | baseLineItemFields, createQuoteLineItem*Schema |\\n| `shared/validations/customer-order.ts:4-20` | customer order line items (flat object, all nullable) | customerOrderLineItemSchema |\\n| `shared/types/repair.ts:86-115` | TypeScript interfaces for repair line items | RepairLineItem, CreatePartLineItemInput, CreateLaborLineItemInput |\\n| `shared/validations/__tests__/quote.test.ts` | Existing test patterns to follow | All 3 types tested |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Archivist \u2014 2026-06-01 (Round 2: Composition Approach Decision)\\n\\n#### Resolution: Use \\\"Loose Base\\\" Pattern (Approach 1)\\n\\nThe PRD (#242) states: **\\\"Each module composes its own discriminated union from shared variants.\\\"** This confirms the loose base pattern \u2014 the shared file exports plain field-definition objects, and each module spreads them into `z.object()` with module-specific overrides.\\n\\nThis is also the **established codebase convention**:\\n- `customer.ts` (line 17): `addressFields` object spread into both `createPrivateSchema` and `createCompanySchema`\\n- `repair.ts` (line 189): `baseLineItemFields` spread into part/labor schemas\\n- `quote.ts` (line 51): `baseLineItemFields` spread into all three variant schemas\\n\\n#### Shared Variants File Structure (`shared/validations/line-item-variants.ts`)\\n\\nThe file should export **plain objects** (not Zod schemas) containing field definitions:\\n\\n```typescript\\n// Base fields shared across ALL line item types\\nexport const baseLineItemFields = {\\n  description: z.string().min(1, 'description is required').max(500),\\n  quantity: z.number().int().positive('quantity must be positive'),\\n  unitPriceNet: z.number().int().nonnegative('unitPriceNet must be non-negative'),\\n  vatRateId: z.string().min(1, 'vatRateId is required'),\\n  discountPercent: z.number().int().min(0).max(10000).nullable().optional(),\\n}\\n\\n// Part variant fields (partId loose \u2014 module overrides for strictness)\\nexport const partVariantFields = {\\n  lineType: z.literal('part'),\\n  partId: z.string().uuid('partId must be a valid UUID').optional().nullable(),\\n}\\n\\n// Labor variant fields\\nexport const laborVariantFields = {\\n  lineType: z.literal('labor'),\\n  laborServiceId: z.string().uuid('laborServiceId must be a valid UUID').optional().nullable(),\\n  minutesWorked: z.number().int().positive().nullable().optional(),\\n  hourlyRateSnapshot: z.number().int().nonnegative().nullable().optional(),\\n}\\n\\n// Bicycle variant fields\\nexport const bicycleVariantFields = {\\n  lineType: z.literal('bicycle'),\\n  bicycleId: z.string().uuid('bicycleId must be a valid UUID').optional().nullable(),\\n  bicycleBrand: z.string().max(100).optional().nullable(),\\n  bicycleModel: z.string().max(200).optional().nullable(),\\n  bicycleYear: z.number().int().min(1900).max(new Date().getFullYear() + 1).optional().nullable(),\\n  bicycleColor: z.string().max(50).optional().nullable(),\\n  bicycleFrameSize: z.string().max(20).optional().nullable(),\\n}\\n```\\n\\n#### Module-Specific Composition Examples\\n\\n**repair.ts** \u2014 tightens partId/laborServiceId to required:\\n```typescript\\nimport { baseLineItemFields, partVariantFields, laborVariantFields } from './line-item-variants.js'\\n\\nexport const createPartLineItemSchema = z.object({\\n  ...baseLineItemFields,\\n  ...partVariantFields,\\n  // Override: tighten partId to required for repairs\\n  partId: z.string().min(1, 'partId is required'),\\n})\\n```\\n\\n**quote.ts** \u2014 uses loose variants as-is (no override needed):\\n```typescript\\nimport { baseLineItemFields, partVariantFields } from './line-item-variants.js'\\n\\nexport const createQuoteLineItemPartSchema = z.object({\\n  ...baseLineItemFields,\\n  ...partVariantFields,\\n})\\n```\\n\\n**customer-order.ts** \u2014 uses flat object (no discriminated union), spreads all variant fields:\\n```typescript\\nimport { baseLineItemFields } from './line-item-variants.js'\\n\\nexport const customerOrderLineItemSchema = z.object({\\n  lineType: z.enum(['part', 'labor', 'bicycle']),\\n  ...baseLineItemFields,\\n  partId: z.string().nullable().optional(),\\n  laborServiceId: z.string().nullable().optional(),\\n  // bicycle fields...\\n})\\n```\\n\\n#### POS (sales.ts) \u2014 Needs Upgrade to Discriminated Union\\n\\nCurrently `cartLineItemSchema` in `shared/validations/sales.ts` only supports parts. The PRD requires upgrading POS to support all three line item types. After shared variants are created, sales.ts should be refactored similarly to repair.ts with strict partId:\\n```typescript\\nexport const posPartLineItemSchema = z.object({\\n  ...baseLineItemFields,\\n  ...partVariantFields,\\n  partId: z.string().min(1, 'partId is required'), // POS requires catalog reference (PRD story #14)\\n})\\n\\nexport const createDirectSaleLineItemSchema = z.discriminatedUnion('lineType', [\\n  posPartLineItemSchema,\\n  posLaborLineItemSchema,\\n  posBicycleLineItemSchema,\\n])\\n```\\n\\n#### Key Decision Summary\\n\\n| Aspect | Decision | Rationale |\\n|--------|----------|-----------|\\n| Composition approach | **Loose base** (plain objects spread into `z.object()`) | Matches PRD language + existing codebase convention in customer.ts/repair.ts/quote.ts |\\n| Shared variant strictness | **All optional/nullable** for entity IDs | Allows each module to tighten as needed; loose base is the natural default |\\n| Module override mechanism | **Spread override** (`{ ...sharedFields, partId: z.string().min(1) }`) | Zod object spread naturally supports field override \u2014 last definition wins |\\n| customer-order.ts pattern | **Flat object** (no discriminated union) | Existing behavior preserved; shared base fields still extracted |\\n\\n#### Files to Modify\\n\\n| File | Action |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `shared/validations/line-item-variants.ts` | **CREATE** \u2014 new file with shared variant field objects |\\n| `shared/validations/repair.ts:189-215` | **REFACTOR** \u2014 import from line-item-variants, remove local baseLineItemFields |\\n| `shared/validations/quote.ts:51-83` | **REFACTOR** \u2014 import from line-item-variants, remove local baseLineItemFields |\\n| `shared/validations/customer-order.ts:4-20` | **REFACTOR** \u2014 import base fields from line-item-variants |\\n| `shared/validations/sales.ts:9-21` | **UPGRADE** \u2014 convert to discriminated union using shared variants (PRD Module 4) |\\n\\n#### Test Strategy\\n\\n- Create `shared/validations/__tests__/line-item-variants.test.ts` for the shared file\\n- Follow patterns from `quote.test.ts` (~250 lines, comprehensive coverage across all 3 types)\\n- Add line item creation tests to `repair.test.ts` (currently missing \u2014 gap identified in Round 1)\\n- Ensure existing tests still pass (no behavior change requirement)\\n\\n<!-- AGENT-FINDINGS-END -->\\n\",\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"Create Shared Line Item Variant Definitions\"}\n"
